= Metacognition — Technical =

== Meta-level architecture ==
Nelson and Narens describe object-level cognition and a meta-level connected by monitoring and control:

<pre>
meta-level
  ↑ monitoring
  ↓ control
object-level cognition
</pre>

The framework is functional; it does not imply a physically separate inner observer.

== Judgments ==
Metacognitive measures include:

* judgments of learning;
* feeling of knowing;
* confidence judgments;
* error detection;
* retrospective confidence.

Calibration, resolution, and bias are different properties of these judgments.

== Signal-detection approaches ==
Metacognitive sensitivity can be analyzed separately from first-order task sensitivity.

Measures such as meta-d' attempt to quantify how well confidence discriminates correct from incorrect decisions while accounting for task performance.

== Control policies ==
Study allocation, information seeking, cognitive offloading, stopping rules, and strategy selection can be modeled as control policies driven by monitoring signals and costs.

